    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0647" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11 Ekvall, Henry/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-21T16:00:00-05:00">November 21, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>372. Your 1254, November 17, 1 p.m., and previous. For your information and
                    encouragement, the Department has suggested to the Chinese Legation here that it
                    inform Nanking that the Department is emphatically interested in and solicitous
                    with regard to this case and that matters relating to this case are being
                    pressed by our representatives in China under express instruction from the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
